<workout_file><author>mywhooshinfo.com</author><name>Low 60&#039;s</name><description>When we complete short steep climbs, the lower cadence results in high crank torque, which recruits more of your fast-twitch fibres. With this in mind, it&#039;s vital that our training meets the demands of this movement. 

Today we are performing lower cadence intervals but with power just above threshold.</description><sportType>bike</sportType><workout>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Often short climbs in racing are performed with a lower than normal cadence."/><textevent timeoffset="60" message="This low rpm, along with high power, results in increased crank torque."/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="High crank torque recruits more of your fast twitch fibers."/><textevent timeoffset="120" message="It&#039;s important that we train these muscle fibers by replicating the demands of low rpm climbing."/><textevent timeoffset="280" message="To continue the warmup we now have a series of 30/30 medium intensity efforts."/></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="5" OnDuration="30" OnPower="0.64999997615814" OffDuration="30" OffPower="0.80000001192093">
</IntervalsT>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Quite often in racing you will be forced out of your comfort zone and need to produce high power at a low cadence."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.80000001192093"><textevent timeoffset="20" message="This should be very comfortable for you."/><textevent timeoffset="80" message="These short high power, low cadence efforts should feel like pushing a weight."/><textevent timeoffset="140" message="As always when there is a target cadence to an interval, focus on hitting that cadence and let the trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="199" message="Remain seated during the intervals and relax your hands on the bars."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="60" Power="0.5"></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="10" OnDuration="120" OnPower="0.75449997186661" OffDuration="60" OffPower="1.0444999933243">
</IntervalsT>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Now for the sting in the tail."/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="Just a quick 5min sub-threshold effort."/><textevent timeoffset="110" message="Let&#039;s get it done!"/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.80000001192093"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="The interesting part here is your chosen cadence."/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="How much have the previous low cadence efforts influenced your cadence here?"/><textevent timeoffset="150" message="Try to spin a little higher than what is comfortable for you here."/><textevent timeoffset="210" message="This is easy for you. This is finishing off a quality workout."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="30" message="Great work today."/><textevent timeoffset="90" message="You may experience some muscle soreness in the coming days from this session."/><textevent timeoffset="110" message="Thats&#039;s a good thing..."/><textevent timeoffset="130" message="Muscle soreness means you have broken the muscle down and it will come back stronger with the appropriate rest."/><textevent timeoffset="200" message="Hydrate and refuel for your next session, starting now."/></SteadyState>
</workout></workout_file>